            "title": "Top notes, heart notes, base notes: the only fragrance guide you need before your next perfume haul",
            "excerpt": "Picture this: you're browsing an online perfume shop at 10pm (as one does), you've found something that sounds absolutely incredible, and the description reads: opens with bergamot and pink pepper, a heart of jasmine and cedarwood, drying down to musk and amber. Gorgeous. But also: what does any of that actually mean? And more to the point, is this going to smell the way you're imagining, or are you about to spend real money on a vibe that ghosts you by noon? It happens with luxury inspired perfumes and niche fragrances alike. Knowing the notes is the fix.\n\nOr maybe this one's more familiar: you tested something at a perfume shop, fell completely in love on the spot, bought it, got home, spritzed it on later, and found yourself wondering by evening what happened to the fragrance you were so certain about six hours ago. Nothing went wrong. You just met top notes, and then you didn't.",
