            "title": "What you are actually paying for in a $300 luxury perfume brand bottle: the real cost breakdown nobody talks about",
            "excerpt": "Walk into Sephora on a Saturday afternoon and an impeccably made-up\nsalesperson will spritz a card, hand it to you, and watch your face for a reaction while a $300 bottle sits on the counter behind them looking like an art piece. It smells incredible. Of course it does. At that price it should. Few people ever stop to ask where the $300 is actually going, because a surprisingly small amount of it is sitting inside the bottle itself.\n\nThis is not a scandal. It is just supply and demand pulled apart and once you see the pieces laid out, luxury perfume pricing starts to make a very different kind of sense. None of it is exactly a secret. It is just spread out across enough different receipts that nobody bothers connecting the dots until someone lays them out in one place.",
