            "title": "America's love of gourmand fragrance: why the best perfume for women now smells like something absolutely delicious",
            "excerpt": "Walk through any department store’s fragrance section and it smells like dessert.\nVanilla, caramel, something that might be tonka bean or might just be a very\nconvincing sugar cookie, and half the bottles on that shelf are doing their best\nimpression of a bakery case. This is not an accident. Somewhere over the last few\nyears, America decided the best perfume for women should smell a little bit like\nsomething you would actually want to eat, and it is not hard to see why.\nThis is not new exactly. What is new is how good it has gotten.",
