            "tag": "",
            "title": "The fragrance gift guide for people who refuse to give boring presents: luxury inspired perfumes sorted by personality, not price",
            "excerpt": "Somewhere in America right now, someone is unwrapping a Bath and Body Works\ngift set for the third year running, smiling the exact smile you give a gift that required\nzero information about the person receiving it. This is not anyone's fault. It is just\nwhat happens when gift shopping turns into a category to check off instead of an\nactual person to think about. Candles, lotion sets, a mug that says something\ngeneric about coffee: all perfectly nice, all instantly forgettable, all grabbed under\npressure in the last aisle of a store that was never the plan.\nFragrance can fix this, but only if you stop shopping by budget and start shopping by\nwho someone actually is. A 20 dollar bottle picked because it is unmistakably them\nwill beat an 80 dollar gift set picked because it was sitting at the Sephora checkout\nline. Here is how to get it right this year, sorted by personality instead of price tag.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/the-fragrance-gift-guide-for-people-who-refuse-to-give-boring-presents-luxury-inspired-perfumes-sorted-by-personality-not-price",
