        "blog_item_9FRjY3": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_scent_of_an_American_summer_Thumbnail_jpg.jpg",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "The scent of an American summer: sunscreenyou swear you applied, a screen door slamming,and the fragrance that ties the whole seasontogether",
            "excerpt": "An American summer starts the second school lets out and does not fully quit until the first\npumpkin flavored latte shows up at the coffee shop and ruins everyone&#39;s denial. In between, it is\none long, sun-drunk stretch of lake days, backyard cookouts, road trips with the windows down,\nand at least one Fourth of July where someone insists they know what they are doing with the fireworks. You mean to reapply the sunscreen. You truly do. Then the game gets competitive,\nthe burgers are ready, and by evening your shoulders are telling a story your memory does not\nfully back up.\nSummer has a smell, and you know it before you can name it. Warm cut grass and charcoal\nsmoke. Sunscreen and chlorine and watermelon eaten over the sink. Hot asphalt right before a\nthunderstorm finally breaks the humidity. A screen door swinging open onto a porch in the\nevening. It is nostalgia you can breathe, and it is doing a lot of quiet emotional work before you\nhave thought about it once.",
            "link": "shopify://blogs/news/the-scent-of-an-american-summer-sunscreen-you-swear-you-applied-a-screen-door-slamming-and-the-fragrance-that-ties-the-whole-season-together",
            "link_label": "Read Article"
          }
        },
        "blog_item_edTkkn": {
          "type": "blog_item",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_13_2026_09_46_58_PM_54c55edf-fe39-4bf4-a3b9-790174f0c05f.png",
            "tag": "",
            "title": "Fragrance layering, explained: how to turn two colognes into a signature scent no one else is wearing",
            "excerpt": "Somewhere in the past couple of years, wearing one fragrance stopped cutting it. Open TikTok\nand inside a minute you'll catch someone double-fisting two bottles like a bartender at happy\nhour, swearing the result is a scent nobody else on the planet is wearing. It looks like a gimmick.\nIt looks like a slick way to sell you twice the cologne. It is neither. Layering is one of the oldest\nplays in a perfumer's book, finally run for the rest of us, and once it clicks you'll wonder why you\nspent years wearing your fragrances one at a time like it was still 1998.",
